#
# sqlplus 11.2's data-type request in the native form (#2466): the charset
# twice, flag 2 (no type table), its compile capabilities (OCI2, index 31, is
# 0xBF, its 0x10 asking for DRCP) and runtime capabilities, the time-zone block,
# the timezone-file version and the national charset.
# Captured 2026-11-05 through tools/capture_proxy.py: sqlplus 11.2 (instant
# client 11.2, x86-64 Linux) logging in to Oracle 11g XE 11.2.0.2 with
# SERVER=POOLED, the DRCP pool started. The TTC payload, without the packet's
# header, as `hexdump -C` output; the offset column and the |ascii| gutter are
# ignored by tests.replay.parse_hexdump.
00000000  02 69 03 69 03 02 27 06  01 01 01 0f 01 01 06 01  |.i.i..'.........|
00000010  01 01 01 01 01 01 7f ff  03 0a 03 07 01 01 7f 01  |................|
00000020  7f ff 01 09 01 01 bf 01  05 06 00 01 07 04 07 02  |................|
00000030  01 00 00 18 00 03 80 00  00 00 3c 3c 3c 80 00 00  |..........<<<...|
00000040  00 00 00 00 0e d0 07                              |.......|
00000047
